<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 17.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Jan 17.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 01/17/97  01/10/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    123.95    142.12    53.30	61.11     38.62</p>
<p>West	    102.11    121.06    39.41	46.72     52.41</p>
<p>Total Canada  226.06    263.17    45.98	53.53     45.89</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 01/17/97: 232.55 bcf, 01/10/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 01/17/97: 259.11 bcf, 01/10/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
